---
description: strata_forge.config — Pydantic Settings root + YAML overlays + .env.
globs: ["src/strata_forge/config/**/*.py", "configs/**", ".env*"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- `Settings` (in `strata_forge.config.settings`) is the single source of truth for runtime configuration. **Do not read env vars directly elsewhere** — go through `strata_forge.config.get_settings()`.
- Provider configs are Pydantic `BaseSettings` subclasses; one per provider, in `strata_forge.llm.providers.config`.
- Loading order (lowest → highest precedence): defaults → YAML overlay (`configs/<FORGE_PROFILE>.yaml`) → `.env` → process env → in-code override.
- `strata-forge doctor` validates settings on every run. When adding a new setting, add a doctor check for it (and a row in `.env.example`).
- Never log a `Settings` instance directly — it contains secrets. Use the redaction helpers.
- `get_settings()` is cached for the lifetime of the process; `reset_settings()` exists for tests only.
